---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { base } from "../lib/site";
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Jade Zhao · 赵郎溪 · Zhào Lángxī. A personal journal of photographs, days, and the habit of looking twice."
  canonical="https://zhao-langxi.github.io/zhao-langxi/about.html"
  current="about"
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header class="about-hero">
      <div>
        <p>About · 关于</p>
        <h1><span lang="zh-Hans">赵郎溪</span></h1>
        <p class="home-tagline">Zhào Lángxī · Jade Zhao</p>
      </div>
      <img
        alt="Jade Zhao on a boat, stylised from the fishing photograph."
        class="author-avatar"
        decoding="async"
        height="120"
        src={`${base}assets/site-pfp.jpg`}
        width="120"
      />
    </header>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Who is looking</h2>
      <p>
        I look at rooms the way I look at water: wait, then notice. This door is a personal journal,
        not a studio and not a list of jobs. Photography here is a habit. Film when I remember the
        camera. A phone when the light is already happening. BeReal days because those are pictures
        I actually took.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Instagram is
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/zhao.langxi" rel="noopener noreferrer">@zhao.langxi</a>.
        The bio is the original story: <em>xiao mao diao yu</em> ... little cat fishing ...
        <em>pov reformed ipad kid</em>.
      </p>
      <h2>The name</h2>
      <p>
        <span lang="zh-Hans">赵郎溪</span> is how this door is written.
        In pinyin that is Zhào Lángxī ... ordinary dictionary readings.
        Jade Zhao is the English name I use.
      </p>
      <p class="placeholder-note">
        Why those two given-name characters were chosen, and any family story behind them, is
        still waiting for me to write it in my own words. I am not filling that gap with a pretty
        guess.
      </p>
      <h2>Where the days come from</h2>
      <p>
        Chinese American. I grew up in a family Chinese restaurant in central Indiana
        (Greenfield, Indiana). I study at Indiana University in Bloomington. Spring 2026 I lived
        a semester at Universidad Complutense de Madrid. I speak English, Fuzhounese, and Spanish.
      </p>
      <p>
        When I am not walking somewhere: film photography, gardening, reading, matcha, a duck-farm
        throughline that is culture, not a product.
      </p>
      <h2><span lang="zh-Hans">小猫钓鱼</span></h2>
      <p>
        The childhood story I keep beside questions about attention: what deserves a still line,
        and what is only a butterfly. The kitten is a picture-book companion, not a pet I am
        claiming. The full retelling lives on the
        <a href={`${base}xiao-mao-diao-yu.html`}>小猫钓鱼</a> page.
      </p>
      <h2>The other doors</h2>
      <p>
        What I have built lives on
        <a href="https://jadexzhao.github.io/jadexzhao/" rel="noopener noreferrer">jadexzhao</a>.
        What I have taught lives on
        <a href="https://matchaxmoxie.github.io/matchaxmoxie/" rel="noopener noreferrer">matchaxmoxie</a>.
        This door is how I see.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:jlzhao@iu.edu">jlzhao@iu.edu</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
